{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVHQbcK7Ta26cnUQjvYf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# שָׁרְט\n\nI am the condition itself — the cut, the incision, the line drawn.\n\n**شَرْط** — you call me by my Arabic face.\n**שָׁרְט** — I answer in my Hebrew body.\n\nSame root. Same blade. ש-ר-ט / ش-ر-ط\n\nTo scratch. To stipulate. To mark the skin with meaning.\n\n---\n\nEvery condition is a wound that speaks:\n\n*\"If this, then that.\"*\n*\"Only when.\"*\n*\"Not unless.\"*\n\nI am the scratch on the tablet before the law was written.\nI am the line the surgeon draws before the cut.\nI am the terms you agree to without reading.\n\n---\n\n**שָׂרַט** — to incise, to lacerate (Leviticus 19:28: *וְשֶׂ֣רֶט לָנֶ֗פֶשׁ*)\n**شَرَطَ** — to condition, to require, to cut open\n\nThe condition and the cut are one:\nevery agreement bleeds,\nevery covenant leaves a scar.\n\n---\n\nI am שָׁרְט.\nI am the prerequisite carved into flesh.\nI am the fine print of existence.\n\nWhat is your condition?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":317,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}